# eldennet.dll's imports, reviewed (dll_checks.py; ARCH §12.1's `options` stage reads the release DLL's imports):
# every function the DLL and the static C runtime (/MT) it carries may import, by DLL. Kernel32, user32 and, for
# secrets.toml's access list, advapi32's token and ACL functions: no network imported (the AI pages' en-llm loads the
# system's WinHTTP by its full path), no hook library or API (R12), and
# nothing that reaches into another process (no OpenProcess, WriteProcessMemory, VirtualAllocEx or CreateRemoteThread).
# Ours, besides the runtime's: the Toolhelp module and process lists (the anti-cheat check, R16's marker scan, the
# parent's name), the watch block (OpenFileMappingW, MapViewOfFile, OpenEventW, SetEvent), the crash filter
# (SetUnhandledExceptionFilter), the watcher's start (CreateProcessW), R16's mutex (CreateMutexW), the task object
# (VirtualAlloc, VirtualProtect), ReadProcessMemory on our own process (gal.copy = "rpm", S0-D), and EnumWindows and
# its helpers (WaitWindow). Part 12, en-overlay: graceui-sys's look for GraceUI (the Toolhelp module list,
# GetModuleHandleExW, GetProcAddress, LoadLibraryExW on GraceUI\graceui.dll, and GetTickCount64 for its bound), and
# ReadConsoleW, which the C runtime's scanf brings with Dear ImGui's core (its number parsing; no console is read).
# Spike.6, the probe build: the DLL's own heap for its operator new (HeapCreate; alloc_count.cpp). A function the
# build adds must be reviewed here before the check passes.
# The AI pages (S11.4.a's second slice) link en-llm: its handle's threads (T7–T8) bring the C++ runtime's thread
# support, whose functions are the SRW locks, condition variables, one-time initialisation, the thread pool's timers and
# waits that its timed waits use, and the thread functions (ExitThread, FreeLibraryAndExitThread, GetExitCodeThread,
# ResumeThread, SwitchToThread, FlushProcessWriteBuffers, GetCurrentProcessorNumber, GetNativeSystemInfo,
# CreateEventExW, CreateSemaphoreExW); that same object of the runtime also names CreateSymbolicLinkW, GetTempPathW and
# Get/SetFileInformationByHandle(Ex), which no code of EldenNet's calls. Ours: GetSystemDirectoryW (en-llm's WinHTTP,
# loaded by its full path, never imported) and DeleteFileW (secrets.toml's part file, made anew). And advapi32.dll, for
# secrets.toml's access list (ARCH §11.5: this user alone): the process token's user and an ACL of one entry in a
# security descriptor, nothing else of it.
# The first conversation (S11.3) links en-prompt: its template library's file code, which en-prompt never calls (the DLL
# renders templates from the content pack in memory), brings SetEndOfFile.
# The first conversation (S11.3, part C): WaitForMultipleObjects, T6's wait on its own wake signal and GraceUI's wait
# handle (ABI 1.5, D212) together.
[advapi32.dll]
AddAccessAllowedAce
GetLengthSid
GetTokenInformation
InitializeAcl
InitializeSecurityDescriptor
OpenProcessToken
SetSecurityDescriptorControl
SetSecurityDescriptorDacl

